INDEPENDENT SPECIFICATION: COMPUTATIONAL-ENTROPY LEAK LANDSCAPE ON SEMIPRIME FACTORS
Role: DESIGNER + ADVERSARY (no heavy compute). Full spec and verification script: /Volumes/git/factoring-connection/codex/scratch/ent_g/entropy_spec.md and /Volumes/git/factoring-connection/codex/scratch/ent_g/verify_entropy_spec.py.

CONTEXT AND FIVE IMMEDIATE ADVERSARIAL WARNINGS FOR CODEX'S PIPELINE
Given N=pq (p<q), H(p|N)=0 information-theoretically, yet any poly(n)-time N-only Boolean test T(N) achieving persistent split-free advantage |Pr[T(N)=Y]-1/2|>=c*n^(-k) would breach all proved barriers (PT, NE1, PS, PT-J, AC0-eps; notes/factorbits_results.md, notes/leakmap_results.md, notes/prim_results.md). Five acute traps in Codex's starting design require mitigation:
1. Small-n universe exhaustion & prime reuse: under top2=True ([3*2^(b-2),2^b)), n=24 (b=12) has ONLY 125 primes and 7,750 semiprimes total (full (2^11,2^12) has 255 primes, 32,385 pairs). Drawing 3x2e5 seeds repeats every N ~77x across splits; at n=32 (1,491 primes, 1.11e6 pairs), each prime is reused 805x (design effect ~65) and 23% of N collide across splits; at n=40, prime reuse is 63x.
2. n=96 power deficit & MI bias: at n=96, delta=1/96^2=1.085e-4 vs SE=1/(2*sqrt(2e5))=1.118e-3 yields E[z]=0.097 (1.29% power, 1-sided alpha=0.01). Detecting 1/96^2 at 80% power requires m>=2.13e8 even for ONE locked survivor; raw plug-in MI has null bias 1/(2m)=2.5e-6 nats, 106x larger than true 2*delta^2=2.35e-8 nats.
3. Log-magnitude OLS trap: fitting log|adv_hat(n)| vs log n on m=2e5 misclassifies a pure 2^(-n/4) exponential leak as polynomial (mean k_hat=4.17) 98.4% of the time because E|adv_hat| floors at sqrt(2/pi)*SE=8.9e-4 for n>=56.
4. Sorting bias p=min(p,q): even for uniform U_1,U_2, min(U_1,U_2) has Pr[bit_j=1]=1/2-2^(-(j+1)) (0.239, 0.368, 0.436 at n=24), giving constant-0 tests O(1) raw advantage Pr[X=Y]-1/2.
5. Size-normalization curvature: linear (p-p_min)/(sqrt(N)-p_min)>=1/2 leaves 0.0431 O(1) size bias at n=96; log-linear 1-ln(q/p)/ln(N/p_min^2)>=1/2 omits 1/(ln p*ln q) PNT curvature, creating a fake Theta(1/n^2) size leak.

1. TEST GRAMMAR BEYOND CODEX'S STARTING LIST
Codex's baseline (1-layer x^N, V_N, 1-shift (x^N+c)^N, basic floors/irrationals, prefix CFs of sqrt(N) and N/2^k, Jacobi/bit/XOR readouts) mostly lies inside proved-null fragments (NE1, PS, PT-J, AC0-eps) or D2's bounded 1-shift fragment. Extend to a typed, gcd-instrumented DAG grammar (types PubInt, ModN, ExtModN, Form, ECPt, LatOut, Bit; <=50us/eval at n=96; 2e4-1e5 tests deduplicated by 64-modulus truth-table hashing) across seven open-frontier families:
- G1 (Open-Frontier PRIM, notes/prim_results.md): (i) >=3-term inner depth-2 (x^N+y^N+c)^N and summed nested gates (x^N+c1)^N+-(y^N+c2)^N (Weil degree ~p, outside D2); (ii) shift-depth>=2 towers with non-torsion targets (((x^N+c1)^N+c2)^N-y^N) mod N and ((x^(2N+1)+c1)^N+c2)^N-3 (escapes small-order peeling and FROZEN/CLOSURE identities); (iii) modular-inverse gates ((x^N+c1)^(-1)+c2)^N mod N (Shparlinski Open Problem 8 exponential Kloosterman sums) and Redei/Chebyshev rational maps; (iv) SLP-compressed powers M_B=prod_{l<=B} l^floor(log_l B) (B in {16,32,64}) in ((x^N+1)^M_B+c)^N, Jacobi ((x^N+c)^M_B-1|N), and compressed (2^(2^k)+c|N) (defeats D2's GRH order hypothesis and J1's height bound); (v) extension coordinates: asymmetric Lucas U_N(P,Q), cubic/quartic Frobenius coordinates in (Z/N)[T]/(T^d-aT-b), and AKS monomial coefficients coeff_j((T+a)^N mod (N,T^r-1)), r in {5,7,11,13} (incomplete sums where p^d-1>>|I|).
- G2 (Class Group Cl(-4kN) & Disc -N/-4kN Forms, notes/genusleak_results.md): for k in {1,2,3,5,7} and small split primes (-4kN|l)=+1, build prime forms f_l=(l,b_l,(b_l^2+kN)/(4l)) and run O(n) NUCOMP steps at exponents EXCEEDING sqrt(N) (fixing classE's trivial l^j<sqrt(N) bug): f_l^N, f_l^(N+-1), f_l^floor(sqrt(N)), f_l^(M_32*2^ceil(n/2)), and f_l1^e1*f_l2^e2>2*sqrt(N) (couples N to h(-4kN)~sqrt(N)L(1,chi) rather than p-1). Read (a_red|N), (a_red|l'), chi_-4(a_red), chi_8(a_red), sgn(b_red), [|b_red|<=a_red/4].
- G3 (Multiplier-Pencil CFs sqrt(kN), Infrastructure Jumps & Class-E Rationals, notes/classE_results.md): (i) CFs of sqrt(kN) (k in {1,2,3,5,6,7,11,13}, T<=64): parity-split counts of Q_i with 7-smooth squarefree core and running (Q_i|l) products; (ii) O(n) real-infrastructure NUCOMP giant steps in Q(sqrt(kN)) to distance D in {floor(N^(1/4)),floor(N^(1/3)),floor(sqrt(N)),N}, reading (Q_D|N) and [Q_D<sqrt(kN)/2]; (iii) Class-E Euclid functionals at moving numerators a(N) in {floor(sqrt(N)), N^(-1) mod floor(sqrt(N)), 2^N mod N, 2^((N-1)/2) mod N, (2^((N-1)/2))^(-1) mod N} (probing open midpoint [N^(7/12),N^(3/4)] and reversed half): Rademacher integer Phi(a/N)=(a+a_bar)/N-12*s(a,N) mod {2,3,4,8}, CF length parity, alternating sum sum(-1)^i*a_i, midpoint certificate ((-1)^k*s_k*r_{k+1}|N) at s_k>=sqrt(N), Manin symbols {oo,a(N)/N} on X_0(11,14,15), and 3D cotangent sums with shift (N-1)/2.
- G4 (Modular / X_0(N) / Torsion-Algebra Cusp Proxies, notes/nativemod_results.md, geometry): (i) #X_0(N)(F_l) fibers via ((t^2-4l|N))_{|t|<2*sqrt(l)} paired with x^(N+-1) mod (N,x^2-tx+l); (ii) literal Frobenius X_N=x^N mod (N,psi_l(x)) on E in {11a1,14a1,37a1}, l in {3,5,7}, reading Tr(X_N^j) and (Res_x(psi_l,X_N-x)|N); (iii) cusp-edge Hurwitz discriminants t^2-4N for t=floor(2*sqrt(N))-j (j=0..7).
- G5 (Small N-Dependent Lattices, dim 3..6, notes/topblock_results.md, leakmap GAR): (i) Coppersmith bases for (floor(sqrt(N))+h) mod N at scale N^(1/4), reading log(||b_d*||/||b_1*||), (b_{1,0}|N), sign patterns; (ii) hidden-phase GAR simultaneous-relation LLL on (N,2^N mod N,3^N mod N,floor(sqrt(N))) probing rep(x)/N==(x_p-x_q)*theta+x_q/N mod 1; (iii) dim-6 prime-log Babai signs.
- G6 (Elliptic-Curve Arithmetic mod N, notes/tracedata_results.md): projective Montgomery ladders on CM, non-CM (11a1,37a1), and N-twisted curves. Since #E(F_p)=p+1-a_p, [N]P=[(a_p-1)q]P on E(F_p), coupling trace a_p with q! Test [N]P, [N+1]P, [N+1-floor(2*sqrt(N))]P, [M_32]P, depth-2 "Elliptic PRIM" (feeding x([N]P)+c into a second [N]P' ladder), degree-2/3 algebra twists, and EDS symbols (Z_N|N).
- G7 (Non-AC0 Circuits & Rep Readouts): dense weight-Theta(n) BCH/QR parities of bits of N, N^2, floor(2^(2n)/N) (AC0[xor], conn_ana H9 OPEN); base-3/5/7 digit sums/parities (NC1 carries); S_3/SL_2(F_3) automata on N's bits; normalized floor(2^k*rep(v)/N) mod 2 and centered popcount(rep(v)); depth-2 XOR/MAJ3 combinators.

2. TARGETS: SIZE-FREE TOP/RATIO BITS AND SANITIZED GL PARITIES
Given N=pq with p in [B_lo,B_hi], exact support is p in [p_min(N),sqrt(N)) where p_min(N)=max(B_lo,N/B_hi), s_min=ln p_min(N).
- Exact PNT Probability-Integral-Transform (size-free top AND p/q ratio bits): under PNT density 1/ln u, Jacobian dq=dN/p gives conditional density of s=ln p proportional to 1/(s*(ln N-s)) on [s_min,(1/2)ln N), with closed-form CDF:
  U_PNT(p|N)=1-ln(ln q/ln p)/ln((ln N-s_min)/s_min) in [0,1)
  (192-bit mpfr; drop boundary sqrt(N)-p_min<16*ln N). Define T_top,k=floor(2^k*U_PNT(p|N)) mod 2 (k=1..4). Because p/q=p^2/N is strictly monotone in p given N, T_top,k simultaneously defines exact size-free top bits of p and ratio bits of p/q; cross-check via empirical quantiles within 4096 N-top-bit bins.
- Sanitized GL parities <r,p> mod 2: enforce r_0=0, zero top max(4,ceil(log2 n)) bits, and require >=4 active bits in [1,floor(b/2)] (prevents 2^(-k) masks from landing purely in size-coupled top bits). Score 8 public masks per n (GL-fixed), 4 PIT-GL parities <r,floor(2^16*U_PNT)>, and instance-varying GL-var ONLY for two-input (N,r_i) controls (Prop GLM).
- Suite (scored on BOTH p_min and coin-flipped random factor p_* in {p,q} to separate symmetric vs p<q orientation leaks): middle bits bit_{floor(b/2)}(p), bit_{floor(b/3)}(p); low-bit sanity controls bit_1..bit_4(p) (keep N=1,3 mod 4 separate for bit_1); genus symbols eps=(-1|p), (2|p), (-3|p), (5|p), (-7|p) strictly on (D|N)=+1; non-genus cubic [p==+-1 mod 7] (N=1 mod 7), quartic [p==1 mod 5|p==+-1 mod 5], and balanced [p mod 3==1], [p mod 5 in {1,2}].

3. STATISTICS PROTOCOL, n=96 SAMPLE SIZES, AND DECAY FIT
- Centered advantage & variance: stratify on H(N)=(N mod 3840, top_10_bits(N)); score adv_perp=(2/m)*sum_h sum_{i in h}(X_i-Xbar_h)(Y_i-Ybar_h), Mantel-Haenszel z_MH (n>=56), and two-way dyadic cluster-robust z_dyad (n<=48). Report Miller-corrected MI and validation log-loss lift.
- Disjoint prime pools & multiple testing (2e5-1e6 pairs): hash primes r into disjoint pools P_disc (30%), P_val (30%), P_conf (40%) so zero primes cross splits (n=24 is finite-census diagnostic only). Screen Discovery via B=1000 within-stratum Westfall-Young max-|Z| permutations (FWER 0.05) on per-n Z and pooled S=sum_{n in {32..56}} w_n*Z_n/sqrt(sum w_n^2) (w_n=n^(-2)*sqrt(m_n/D_eff,n)). Promote <=64 hits to Validation (split_free, Holm 0.01, strata N mod (2^12*105) x top_12(N)) to lock survivors K_2 and signs s_{p,t}; test K_2 once on Confirmation (1-sided Holm 0.01).
- Sample sizes for delta=1/n^2 at n=96: exact m=(z_crit+z_pow)^2*n^4/4 gives (80% power): m=1.67e8 (single, 2-sided 0.05), m=2.13e8 (single locked survivor, 1-sided 0.01; 2.76e8 at 90% power), m=3.63e8 (20 survivors, Holm 0.01), and m=8.41e8 (2e5-pair de-novo FWER 0.01); delta=1/n needs m=23,124 (single) or 91,241 (de-novo). On m=2e5, n=96 MDE is 3.54e-3=32.6/n^2: plant 1/n, 16/n^2, and 1/n^2 controls, reserving heavy C/GMP confirmation for <=3 stage-2 survivors.
- Decay fit (signed linear WLS, NEVER log|adv|): fit y_n=s_{p,t}*adv_perp,conf(n) on n in {32,40,48,56,64,80,96} weighted by 1/sigma_n^2 against M_poly (C*n^(-k), 0<k<=6), M_exp_bar (A*2^(-beta*n), beta>=1/6 covering NE1/cov/SQUFOF), M_exp_free (beta>=0.02), and M_sub (A*exp(-gamma*sqrt(n*ln n))). At m=1e8/size, 1/n^2 gives noiseless dChi2=105.2 vs M_exp_bar (82% power, 0% FP) but 3.36 vs free 2^(-0.064n) and 1.14 vs M_sub (add n=128 if triggered). Lead requires ALL four: (C1) split_free z_conf(80)>=3 and z_conf(96)>=3; (C2) chi2(M_exp_bar)-chi2(M_poly)>=9.21 (unambiguous poly iff min(chi2(M_exp_free),chi2(M_sub))-chi2(M_poly)>=6.63); (C3) chi2(M_poly)<=15.09 and slope k_hi[64,96]-k_lo[32,56]<=2*SE; (C4) <20% shift at n>=64 excluding splits.

4. LEAKAGE AND ARTIFACT CHECKLIST
- Splits: flag gcd(v,N) in {p,q} on every residue PLUS harness budget splits (|q-p|<=4*B_step*N^(1/4) Fermat/Lehman, CF squares Q_2i=r^2 causing |z|=34.1 in leakmap E2, p+-1 B_step-smoothness); report split_free and all.
- Size & sorting p<q: U_PNT(p|N) + 10-bit N-top strata + centered adv_perp + 0.1% boundary trim + p_min vs random p_* + negative controls (isqrt(N), frac(sqrt(N))).
- CRT & Chebyshev imbalance: b=12 top2 Pr[eps=1]=0.4597; b=16 Pr[QR_2=1]=0.5194; killed by N mod 3840 strata + degenerate floor checks.
- Prime-gap bias: gmpy2.next_prime shifts 16-bit Pr[p==1 mod 3] from 0.5010 to 0.4763 and inflates p-1 smoothness; strictly use uniform odd rejection.
- PRNG, float53 & FROZEN/CLOSURE: float64 drops low bits of N for n>=56 (use integer/192-bit mpfr, SHA-256 RNGs, AST isolation); symbolically filter r in {-2..2} identities and verify ord_p(x)>64.

5. THEORETICAL PRIOR PER TEST FAMILY (SPLIT-FREE ADVANTAGE)
- Provably null / superpoly-null: Pure SLPs, fixed p+-1/ECM/rho -> exact 0 (Theorem PT/PT-m/PT2). Fixed-arg Jacobi/Artin/Dedekind/mult-automata -> O(e^(-c*n^d)) uncond., O(2^(-n/4)) GRH (Theorem RA, PT-J1, Theorem L). AC0 & polylog Walsh parities vs eps -> O(n^(-C)) uncond. (Theorem AC0-eps; false on size targets). 1-layer N-gates (NE1), sparse sums (PS), fresh-coin chains (R-chain), bounded-height fresh Jacobi (J1) -> <=2^(-n/6+o(1)) via (M) cosets and (A) pins.
- Open (conjectured 0 or 2^(-Omega(n)) split-free): Deterministic PRIM depth>=2 (D2 leaves C*delta exceptional primes and fails on SLP bases 2^M_B; >=3-term inner, shift-depth>=2 non-torsion, inverse gates, deterministic/compressed Jacobi open). CF of sqrt(kN) & infrastructure -> PROVED non-zero Theta(poly(n)*2^(-n/4)) genus leak on eps/(l|p), CONJECTURED 0 on non-genus targets (H-GEN). Cl(-4kN) coefficients (generic walks O(q^3/X) by GB/GIRTH; arithmetic readouts open). Class-E a(N)/N midpoint [N^(7/12),N^(3/4)] & reversed half (F-SQ covers <=N^(7/12)). Torsion algebras x^N mod psi_l & EC [N]P=[(a_p-1)q]P ladders (X_0(N)(F_l) is QR-type; extension/elliptic PRIM open). Small N-lattices & rep readouts / AC0[xor] / base-3,5 carries (Turing-complete via REP-C; window lattices capped at N^(1/4) by Prop T).
